Subject: [PATCH] signin: honor background networking suppression for account metrics

Base: Chromium 155.0.8059.84
Source-Base: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chromium/chromium/155.0.8059.84/
Original-SHA256: 8658a78b2fa2e09b846c1f8d1ae2b05fd214b95bcb35e656f5aa348d3a0db8d9  chrome/browser/signin/BUILD.gn
Original-SHA256: 9259dfdb9b0d2d39af42dc77515740fe3f4a17c2de6f78c18bb8a24c8e4bd8a6  chrome/browser/signin/account_investigator_factory.cc
Reference-SHA256: e73e2db1257bdafe37216df4315d330976d03545e95ca3c52333763879537bfa  chrome/common/chrome_switches.h
Reference-SHA256: cbf3b87b865bf44777757d2702cb15372e00ffc763b271608f190b71eb6ac2ab  chrome/common/BUILD.gn

Skip only the metrics service when --disable-background-networking is set.
Keep IdentityManager and its cookie service dependencies unchanged. Gate before
Initialize() can start the overdue periodic ListAccounts report. Without the
switch, preserve eager creation, observation and periodic reporting.

Add a parameterized browser regression using the production factory and real
cookie service with a test ListAccounts response. Check eager timer startup,
nullable lookup, cookie availability and on-change metrics in both switch modes.
Browser tests add default switches after SetUpCommandLine(), so adjust this
switch in SetUpDefaultCommandLine() instead. Tests have not been run.

